  "term": "xenophobia",
  "definition": "Xenophobia is an intense or unreasonable fear or dislike of what is perceived as strange or foreign, especially people seen as outsiders or foreigners. It is a hostile attitude that can involve prejudice and rejecting, excluding, or vilifying people because they are viewed as not belonging to the community or national group.",
